[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hello,</p>\n<p>I'm trying to formalize parts of \"Algebraic Identities for Program Calculation\" by Bird in order to learn Lean a bit better.</p>\n<p>The paper contains</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>if the operator ⊕ is associative with identity element a, then</p>\n<p>foldr (⊕) a = foldl (⊕) a</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Which I translated into</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">example</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List.foldr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m.mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List.foldl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m.mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">List.foldr_eq_foldl</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I found that Lean already has a <code>List.foldr_eq_foldl</code> theorem. But I was struggling to apply it. It fails with:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synthesize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Associative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mul</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul</span>\n<span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">synthesize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">LawfulIdentity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mul</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>After some struggling I was able to figure out the issue. Or at least this is my interpretation of the issue.</p>\n<p>Monoid should have the Associative and LawfulIdentity via Semigroup.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Semigroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulOneClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Semigroup.to_isLawfulIdentity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std.LawfulIdentity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Semigroup.to_isAssociative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std.Associative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">mul_assoc</span><span class=\"o\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But Lean fails to match on it, because I use <code>Mul.mul</code> but the <code>instance</code>'s uses <code>(· * ·)</code>. These are definitionally equal but not syntactically equal.</p>\n<p>The fix is to add </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std.Associative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mul.mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">assoc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">m.mul_assoc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Std.LawfulIdentity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mul.mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">left_id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m.one_mul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">right_id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m.mul_one</span>\n<span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Or change the example to </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">example</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List.foldr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List.foldl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">List.foldr_eq_foldl</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is this an accurate diagnoses of the issue?</p>\n<p>So a small syntactical differences can prevent some of the automatic machinery to apply. This seems to imply that some syntax is preferred or is better supported.</p>\n<p>So is there a syntactical conversion that minimize these mismatches in practice?</p>",
        "id": 594660945,
        "sender_full_name": "IsaacDynamo",
        "timestamp": 1778613889
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>List.foldr (· * ·) 1 as = List.foldl (· * ·) 1 as</code> is the correct statement</p>",
        "id": 594671282,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1778617043
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>Mul.mul</code> is basically an implementation detail</p>",
